    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="0925" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163 Property/116</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3614</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-12">June 12, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        13.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the Legation’s
                    despatch No. 3294 of January 21, 1935,<anchor n="47" xml:id="d818-f1"/>
                    concerning the reregistration of land titles at Tsinan, and to enclose for the
                    Department’s records a copy of despatch No. 146 of June 4, 1935,<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d818-f2"/> from Consul Stevens, containing a report of subsequent
                    developments in the matter.</p>
                <p>Although it will be noted that the Land Bureau at Tsinan continues to request
                    that the Seventh Day Adventist Mission be instructed to present its title deed
                    to land in the Commercial Port Area for examination, Consul Stevens states in
                    his latest despatch that the Mayor of Tsinan has orally informed him of his
                    decision to drop the matter for the time being.</p>
                <p>In order to complete the record there is also enclosed a copy of the Legation’s
                    instruction of today’s date to the Consul at Tsinan.<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d818-f3"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Trusler
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d818-f1" n="47" xml:id="d818-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d818-f2" n="47" xml:id="d818-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d818-f3" n="48" xml:id="d818-f3-content">
                <p>The Minister stated therein that he was gratified to learn that the Mayor of
                    Tsinan had decided to drop the matter for the time being.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
